      "id": "d5f0hxt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Difference between Fundamental Rights and DPSP"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "DPSPs are non-justiciable, unlike Fundamental Rights which are enforceable under Article 32 and Article 226.",
        "Article 40 (Organisation of Village Panchayats) and Article 44 (Uniform Civil Code) are among the most frequently tested articles in competitive exams.",
        "In the Minerva Mills Case (1980), the Supreme Court ruled that the Indian Constitution is founded on the bedrock of the balance between Part III (FRs) and Part IV (DPSPs)."
      ],
      "id": "a2e993d"
    },
